{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/646040-discipline-conditions-or-banes","id":646040,"title":"Discipline Conditions or Banes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-30T16:34:32-07:00","id":646040,"title":"Discipline Conditions or Banes","content":"Background: Once upon a time there was a networked LARP(OWoD Vampire) in a city centrally located between Nashville, Atlanta, &amp; Birmingham.<br /> Somebody hit an elder(Thanatos) with power to trigger a frenzy. The call went out for gangrel who had Quell the Beast.<br /> Not one gangrel in the city had a dot of Animalism. Oh they all had celerity to high levels and potence but no animalism.<br /> It took a nos to save the night.<br /> <br /> That always bugged me as player and ST.<br /> So when I saw Discipline derangements in DA revised I was intrigued. I hear it originally popped up in guide to high clans perils of power.<br /> One of the things that triggered them was having out of clans higher than in clans.<br /> <br /> I was wondering would you use conditions to reimplement that or banes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T18:53:22-07:00","id":646181,"title":"","content":"What's a discipline derangement?<br /> <br /> I've little experience with the system, am waiting for the book from the KS instead of reading the pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T19:06:01-07:00","id":646191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/646040-discipline-conditions-or-banes?p=646181#post646181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a discipline derangement?<br /> <br /> I've little experience with the system, am waiting for the book from the KS instead of reading the pdf.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a flaw or weakness introduced OWoD Dark Ages.<br /> This site under general rules seems to have the gist of it.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.stryck.com/DarkAges/HouseRules\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://wiki.stryck.com/pub/skins/gemini/images/NinjaPunchesShark.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.stryck.com/DarkAges/HouseRules\" target=\"_blank\"> House Rules &lt; DarkAges | Stryck Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.stryck.com/DarkAges/HouseRules\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wiki.stryck.com/DarkAges/HouseRules </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thinking of cribbing something similar with conditions and the permanent flaws would be a bane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>I use <a href=\"http://wiki.stryck.com/DarkAges/Disciplines\" target=\"_blank\">Disciplines</a> Curses. A rating of 4 or more in a <a href=\"http://wiki.stryck.com/DarkAges/Disciplines\" target=\"_blank\">Disciplines</a> may impose some penalty on the vampire. This idea was introduced in the Player's Guides to High Clans under the section Perils of Power. Remember: vampirism is a curse.<ul><li>Any vampire who meets <b>3</b> or more of the criteria for Discipline Derangements gains a Temporary Derangement.</li> <li>Any vampire who meets <b>5</b> or more of the criteria for Discipline Derangements gains a <b>Permanent</b>Derangement.<ul><li>Criteria<ul><li>One Clan Discipline has more dots than the other two combined</li> <li>An out-of-Clan Discipline has more dots than any Clan Discipline</li> <li>Knowing multiple powers of the same level( I think they mean elder level)</li> <li>Reaching your maximum potential in a Discipline without at least 5 in another</li> <li>Reaching your maximum potential in a Discipline (yes, it counts twice)</li> <li>Multiple recent botches of a Discipline</li> <li>Multiple recent excessive success with a Discipline</li> <li>Using a Discipline frequently, even when not required</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new 